#BringBackOurSubsidy: WHO IS THIS ECONOMY BEING REFORMED FOR?

A government that makes fuel, food, transportation, electricity and production more expensive, while millions of Nigerians watch their incomes collapse, cannot simply call the suffering “reform.”

THAT IS NOT DEVELOPMENT. THIS IS ECONOMIC PUNISHMENT!

Look at history.

The nations lecturing Nigeria about “free markets” did NOT build their economies by sitting back and allowing their industries to die.

They protected industries.
They subsidised production.
They invested massively in infrastructure.
They supported farmers.
They built human capital.
They used government policy to build national champions.

NOW THEY WANT NIGERIA TO BELIEVE THAT ALL OF THAT IS WRONG?

NO!

The IMF and World Bank may offer advice, but they do not own Nigeria’s future.

Nigeria must stop behaving as though Washington, London or international financial institutions must approve our economic decisions before we act.

🇳🇬 WE ARE A SOVEREIGN NATION.

Our farmers need support—not punishment.

Our manufacturers need affordable energy—not strangling production costs.

Our workers need rising incomes—not collapsing purchasing power.

Our young people need jobs—not endless promises.

Our rural communities need roads, irrigation, electricity, schools and healthcare—not abandonment.

A NATION THAT CANNOT FEED, EMPLOY AND PRODUCE FOR ITS OWN PEOPLE CANNOT REFORM ITS WAY INTO PROSPERITY.

1. We need PRODUCTION.

2. We need INDUSTRIALISATION.

3. We need AGRICULTURAL REVOLUTION.

4. We need PRODUCTIVE SUBSIDIES.

5. We need STRATEGIC NATIONAL ECONOMIC POLICY.

And above all, we need leaders who will put NIGERIA FIRST.

Stop telling Nigerians to endure poverty today for a prosperity that never arrives.

Nigerians deserve an economy that works for Nigerians.

🔥 BRING BACK PRODUCTIVE SUBSIDIES!
🔥 BUILD NIGERIAN INDUSTRY!
🔥 SUPPORT NIGERIAN FARMERS!
🔥 PROTECT NIGERIAN PRODUCTION!

🇳🇬 Nigeria Farms or Nigeria Dies.

