Zanu‑PF Women’s League in Masvingo has concluded its preparations for the 23rd National People’s Conference, adopting resolutions at an inter‑district meeting in Gutu. Provincial Chairwoman Cde Alginia Mhlanga said the proposals include free prenatal care, fair inclusion of women in recruitment for the army, nursing and police, and greater transparency in scholarship allocations.

She emphasised that the process must reflect grassroots voices, noting that the conference offers women a platform to present challenges to a “listening president.” The resolutions will now be forwarded for debate at the national gathering in Mashonaland West this October.
